      <data key="d10">EXPERIMENTAL</data>
      <data key="d11">Participants enrolled within 7 days of an acute coronary syndrome (ACS), who have undergone cardiac catheterization with percutaneous intervention (PCI) or who are being managed conservatively with or without catheterization, and who are receiving antiplatelet therapy standard-of-care (single antiplatelet therapy \[SAPT\] or dual antiplatelet therapy \[DAPT\]) as determined by the investigator will receive milvexian 25 milligrams (mg), orally, twice daily.</data>
