    <node id="DEV:data_access:1">
      <data key="d0">tmkg:DevelopmentEvent</data>
      <data key="d1">GRADUATE I / II</data>
      <data key="d33">data_access</data>
      <data key="d34">GRADUATE I / II</data>
      <data key="d35">Trial investigators state that qualified researchers may request participant-level data via Vivli.</data>
      <data key="d36">Sponsor review; dataset contents and current eligibility must be confirmed.</data>
      <data key="d37">["https://alz-journals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/alz.70192"]</data>
      <data key="d9">biolink:InformationContentEntity</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEV:data_access:2">
      <data key="d0">tmkg:DevelopmentEvent</data>
      <data key="d1">A4</data>
      <data key="d33">data_access</data>
      <data key="d34">A4</data>
      <data key="d35">Official A4/LEARN portal offers registration for data downloads; LONI data-use agreement.</data>
      <data key="d36">Data products include screening, clinical and imaging resources; confirm the exact longitudinal/treatment-arm files required. Registration is not unrestricted anonymous access.</data>
      <data key="d37">["https://www.a4studydata.org/", "https://ida.loni.usc.edu/collaboration/access/appApply.jsp?project=A4"]</data>
      <data key="d9">biolink:InformationContentEntity</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEV:data_access:3">
      <data key="d0">tmkg:DevelopmentEvent</data>
      <data key="d1">PASADENA</data>
      <data key="d33">data_access</data>
      <data key="d34">PASADENA</data>
      <data key="d35">Trial investigators’ secondary-analysis paper includes a patient-level request statement.</data>
      <data key="d36">Does not establish that PADOVA is already available.</data>
      <data key="d37">["https://www.nature.com/articles/s41591-024-02886-y"]</data>
      <data key="d9">biolink:InformationContentEntity</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEV:data_access:4">
      <data key="d0">tmkg:DevelopmentEvent</data>
      <data key="d1">PIVOT IO-001</data>
      <data key="d33">data_access</data>
      <data key="d34">PIVOT IO-001</data>
      <data key="d35">Biomarker paper identifies a qualified-researcher BMS request route.</data>
      <data key="d36">Paper explicitly says data are not publicly available; requests are reviewed. Clinical IPD does not automatically include every omics file.</data>
      <data key="d37">["https://www.nature.com/articles/s41698-024-00641-7"]</data>
      <data key="d9">biolink:InformationContentEntity</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEV:data_access:5">
      <data key="d0">tmkg:DevelopmentEvent</data>
      <data key="d1">TULIP-1</data>
      <data key="d33">data_access</data>
      <data key="d34">TULIP-1</data>
      <data key="d35">Pooled TULIP analysis identifies access through Vivli.</data>
      <data key="d36">Request approval and permitted reuse apply.</data>
      <data key="d37">["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9213795/"]</data>
      <data key="d9">biolink:InformationContentEntity</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEV:data_access:6">
      <data key="d0">tmkg:DevelopmentEvent</data>
      <data key="d1">METREO</data>
      <data key="d33">data_access</data>
      <data key="d34">METREO</data>
      <data key="d35">METREX/METREO analysis includes a data-sharing statement; METREO registry describes proposal approval.</data>
      <data key="d36">Access by request; METREX is not included in the failed-trial denominator.</data>
      <data key="d37">["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8215850/", "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT02105961"]</data>
      <data key="d9">biolink:InformationContentEntity</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEV:data_access:7">
      <data key="d0">tmkg:DevelopmentEvent</data>
      <data key="d1">AMARANTH — derived resources</data>
      <data key="d33">data_access</data>
      <data key="d34">AMARANTH — derived resources</data>
      <data key="d35">Cambridge research repository provides data_notebooks.zip and analysis code.</data>
      <data key="d36">This is an associated research artifact, not verified as the complete sponsor clinical database.</data>
      <data key="d37">["https://www.repository.cam.ac.uk/items/3dca61d5-ce6e-41b6-b613-af21f2dfaa8c"]</data>
      <data key="d9">biolink:InformationContentEntity</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEV:post_failure:1">
      <data key="d0">tmkg:DevelopmentEvent</data>
      <data key="d1">Anifrolumab</data>
      <data key="d33">post_failure</data>
      <data key="d38">Anifrolumab; AstraZeneca</data>
      <data key="d39">TULIP-1 missed SRI-4, a composite lupus response measure.</data>
      <data key="d40">Evaluation showed a more favorable response using BICLA, an alternative measure already collected in the program.</data>
      <data key="d41">AstraZeneca chose BICLA for TULIP-2 after evaluating TULIP-1.</data>
      <data key="d42">TULIP-2 succeeded; Saphnelo received US approval in 2021. Strong example of learning from failure and confirming a revised endpoint in another trial, not retroactively converting TULIP-1 into a success.</data>
      <data key="d37">["https://www.astrazeneca.com/media-centre/press-releases/2019/anifrolumab-phase-iii-trial-meets-primary-endpoint-in-systemic-lupus-erythematosus-29082019.html", "https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/appletter/2021/761123Orig1s000ltr.pdf"]</data>
      <data key="d9">biolink:InformationContentEntity</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEV:post_failure:2">
      <data key="d0">tmkg:DevelopmentEvent</data>
      <data key="d1">Tominersen</data>
      <data key="d33">post_failure</data>
      <data key="d38">Tominersen; Roche/Ionis</data>
      <data key="d39">GENERATION HD1 had an unfavorable overall benefit–risk result.</data>
      <data key="d40">Exploratory post hoc analyses suggested a possible better profile in younger patients with less disease burden and lower exposure.</data>
      <data key="d41">GENERATION HD2 was designed to test lower doses in an earlier/younger population.</data>
      <data key="d42">Directly documented population-and-dose redesign. The subgroup signal was hypothesis-generating; it does not establish efficacy.</data>
      <data key="d37">["https://medically.gene.com/content/dam/pdmahub/restricted/neurology/factor-h-2022/FACTOR-H-2022-presentation-ciriano-update-on-tominersen-clinical-trials.pdf"]</data>
      <data key="d9">biolink:InformationContentEntity</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEV:post_failure:3">
      <data key="d0">tmkg:DevelopmentEvent</data>
      <data key="d1">Prasinezumab</data>
      <data key="d33">post_failure</data>
      <data key="d38">Prasinezumab; Roche/Prothena</data>
      <data key="d39">PASADENA missed its global primary measure; PADOVA later narrowly missed its primary endpoint.</data>
      <data key="d40">PASADENA exploratory analyses suggested greater motor effects in faster progressors. PADOVA had supportive trends and a nominal signal in a prespecified levodopa subgroup.</data>
      <data key="d41">Roche announced advancement to phase III in June 2025 using the total evidence.</data>
      <data key="d42">Development continuation/redesign, not a demonstrated clinical rescue. The PADOVA subgroup was prespecified, so it should not be described as a purely post hoc finding.</data>
      <data key="d37">["https://www.nature.com/articles/s41591-024-02886-y", "https://www.roche.com/media/releases/med-cor-2025-06-16"]</data>
      <data key="d9">biolink:InformationContentEntity</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEV:post_failure:4">
      <data key="d0">tmkg:DevelopmentEvent</data>
      <data key="d1">Lanabecestat</data>
      <data key="d33">post_failure</data>
      <data key="d38">Lanabecestat; trial sponsors, Cambridge researchers, potential trial-design vendors</data>
      <data key="d39">AMARANTH was negative in its broad trial population.</data>
      <data key="d40">A 2025 retrospective AI analysis stratified progression using baseline biomarkers; authors reported 46% less cognitive decline in a selected slow-progressing subgroup at 50 mg.</data>
      <data key="d41">Published a candidate enrichment strategy plus associated data/code.</data>
      <data key="d42">Research proof of concept. No sponsor restart, prospective replication or approval attributable to this finding was verified. The 46% is a selected retrospective estimate, not established treatment efficacy.</data>
      <data key="d37">["https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-025-61355-3"]</data>
      <data key="d9">biolink:InformationContentEntity</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEV:post_failure:5">
      <data key="d0">tmkg:DevelopmentEvent</data>
      <data key="d1">Aducanumab</data>
      <data key="d33">post_failure</data>
      <data key="d38">Aducanumab; Biogen/Eisai</data>
      <data key="d39">Both phase III studies stopped after an interim futility analysis.</data>
      <data key="d40">A larger data cut made EMERGE positive; exposure-related analyses were offered to explain discordant ENGAGE results.</data>
      <data key="d41">Biogen reversed the abandonment decision and submitted for approval.</data>
      <data key="d42">Accelerated US approval followed in 2021, based on amyloid reduction; Biogen discontinued development/commercialization in 2024. Regulatory revival did not establish durable commercial success or validate every post hoc argument.</data>
      <data key="d37">["https://investors.biogen.com/news-releases/news-release-details/biogen-plans-regulatory-filing-aducanumab-alzheimers-disease", "https://investors.biogen.com/news-releases/news-release-details/biogen-realign-resources-alzheimers-disease-franchise"]</data>
      <data key="d9">biolink:InformationContentEntity</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEV:post_failure:6">
      <data key="d0">tmkg:DevelopmentEvent</data>
      <data key="d1">Mepolizumab</data>
      <data key="d33">post_failure</data>
      <data key="d38">Mepolizumab; GSK</data>
      <data key="d39">METREO was negative after multiplicity adjustment; the broader COPD evidence was inconsistent.</data>
      <data key="d40">Pooled METREX/METREO evidence supported greater benefit with higher eosinophils. The meta-analysis was prespecified and included exploratory modeling.</data>
      <data key="d41">Further development focused on eosinophilic COPD; MATINEE subsequently confirmed benefit.</data>
      <data key="d42">US COPD approval in May 2025. A biomarker-enrichment development story with prospective confirmation, not purely a post hoc rescue.</data>
      <data key="d37">["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34163157/", "https://www.gsk.com/en-gb/media/press-releases/gsk-announces-positive-results-from-phase-iii-trial-of-nucala-mepolizumab-in-copd/", "https://www.gsk.com/en-gb/media/press-releases/nucala-mepolizumab-approved-by-us-fda/"]</data>
      <data key="d9">biolink:InformationContentEntity</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEV:post_failure:7">
      <data key="d0">tmkg:DevelopmentEvent</data>
      <data key="d1">Tofersen</data>
      <data key="d33">post_failure</data>
      <data key="d38">Tofersen; Biogen/Ionis</data>
      <data key="d39">VALOR missed the short-duration clinical primary endpoint.</data>
      <data key="d40">Neurofilament light reduction and longer follow-up supplied additional biological and clinical context.</data>
      <data key="d41">Pursued accelerated approval using plasma neurofilament light as a surrogate, alongside further testing.</data>
      <data key="d42">FDA accelerated approval in April 2023 for SOD1-ALS. A biomarker/regulatory strategy; not proof that post hoc clinical analysis made the original primary result positive.</data>
      <data key="d37">["https://www.fda.gov/drugs/news-events-human-drugs/fda-approves-treatment-amyotrophic-lateral-sclerosis-associated-mutation-sod1-gene", "https://www.fda.gov/media/186135/download"]</data>
      <data key="d9">biolink:InformationContentEntity</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEV:post_failure:8">
      <data key="d0">tmkg:DevelopmentEvent</data>
      <data key="d1">Dalcetrapib</data>
      <data key="d33">post_failure</data>
      <data key="d38">Dalcetrapib; DalCor</data>
      <data key="d39">Historical dal-OUTCOMES failed in 2012, outside this review’s failure window.</data>
      <data key="d40">Retrospective pharmacogenomics suggested an ADCY9-defined responder group.</data>
      <data key="d41">A genotype-selected phase III trial, dal-GenE, tested the hypothesis; its 2022 readout is inside the window.</data>
      <data key="d42">dal-GenE still missed the primary intention-to-treat endpoint. A valuable counterexample: plausible post hoc precision-medicine findings may not confirm.</data>
      <data key="d37">["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35856777/"]</data>
      <data key="d9">biolink:InformationContentEntity</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEV:repurposing:1">
      <data key="d0">tmkg:DevelopmentEvent</data>
      <data key="d1">Elafibranor</data>
      <data key="d33">repurposing</data>
      <data key="d43">Elafibranor</data>
      <data key="d44">GENFIT moved emphasis from failed NASH development to primary biliary cholangitis (PBC), later licensed to Ipsen.</data>
      <data key="d45">Iqirvo received accelerated US approval in June 2024. GENFIT reported eligibility for a €48.7 million first-US-sale milestone and tiered royalties up to 20%.</data>
      <data key="d46">Positive PBC phase II data existed in December 2018, before the 2020 NASH failure. This is a genuine indication pivot, but the reviewed evidence does not show it was discovered by post hoc RESOLVE-IT analysis.</data>
      <data key="d47">["https://ir.genfit.com/news-releases/news-release-details/genfit-positive-phase-2-results-study-elafibranor-primary", "https://www.ipsen.com/press-release/ipsens-iqirvo-receives-u-s-fda-accelerated-approval-as-a-first-in-class-ppar-treatment-for-primary-biliary-cholangitis/", "https://ir.genfit.com/news-releases/news-release-details/genfit-historic-milestone-achieved-us-fda-accelerated-approval", "https://www.bayer.com/media/en-us/oceanic-af-study-stopped-early-due-to-lack-of-efficacy/", "https://www.bayer.com/en/us/news-stories/oceanic-stroke", "https://www.amylyx.com/pipeline"]</data>
      <data key="d9">biolink:InformationContentEntity</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEV:repurposing:2">
      <data key="d0">tmkg:DevelopmentEvent</data>
      <data key="d1">Asundexian</data>
      <data key="d33">repurposing</data>
      <data key="d43">Asundexian</data>
      <data key="d44">OCEANIC-AF failed; development in secondary stroke prevention continued.</data>
      <data key="d45">Bayer reported positive OCEANIC-STROKE topline results in November 2025.</data>
      <data key="d46">The stroke study was already running and explicitly continued at the time of the AF stop. Do not attribute it to a later post hoc discovery.</data>
      <data key="d47">["https://ir.genfit.com/news-releases/news-release-details/genfit-positive-phase-2-results-study-elafibranor-primary", "https://www.ipsen.com/press-release/ipsens-iqirvo-receives-u-s-fda-accelerated-approval-as-a-first-in-class-ppar-treatment-for-primary-biliary-cholangitis/", "https://ir.genfit.com/news-releases/news-release-details/genfit-historic-milestone-achieved-us-fda-accelerated-approval", "https://www.bayer.com/media/en-us/oceanic-af-study-stopped-early-due-to-lack-of-efficacy/", "https://www.bayer.com/en/us/news-stories/oceanic-stroke", "https://www.amylyx.com/pipeline"]</data>
      <data key="d9">biolink:InformationContentEntity</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEV:repurposing:3">
      <data key="d0">tmkg:DevelopmentEvent</data>
      <data key="d1">AMX0035</data>
      <data key="d33">repurposing</data>
      <data key="d43">AMX0035</data>
      <data key="d44">After the ALS failure, Amylyx continued work in Wolfram syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d45">The program addresses a different rare neurodegenerative/endocrine disease.</data>
      <data key="d46">Parallel mechanistic/clinical work is not evidence that a PHOENIX post hoc subgroup revealed Wolfram efficacy. PHOENIX’s CENTAUR-like subgroup was also negative.</data>
      <data key="d47">["https://ir.genfit.com/news-releases/news-release-details/genfit-positive-phase-2-results-study-elafibranor-primary", "https://www.ipsen.com/press-release/ipsens-iqirvo-receives-u-s-fda-accelerated-approval-as-a-first-in-class-ppar-treatment-for-primary-biliary-cholangitis/", "https://ir.genfit.com/news-releases/news-release-details/genfit-historic-milestone-achieved-us-fda-accelerated-approval", "https://www.bayer.com/media/en-us/oceanic-af-study-stopped-early-due-to-lack-of-efficacy/", "https://www.bayer.com/en/us/news-stories/oceanic-stroke", "https://www.amylyx.com/pipeline"]</data>
      <data key="d9">biolink:InformationContentEntity</data>
    </node>
